Waycar patch for libssh2 c7557852f1b7c0d3b9cffd5390eb33fdf93fb17f.

packet: keep waiting when a wanted packet belongs to another channel

ssh2_packet_requirev() reads packets until one of the wanted types
arrives, then assumes it is the caller's: when the caller filters by
channel (match_buf) and the packet is another channel's reply of the same
type, packet_askv() finds nothing and requirev returns -1, failing a
wait that should have continued. With one request in flight per session
that never happens; with several channels waiting for replies of the
same type (pipelined opens, overlapping channel requests) it fails
whichever waiter reads the other's reply.

Keep reading instead. The foreign packet stays queued for its owner.
Callers without a match filter are unaffected: any packet of a wanted
type matches them.

diff --git a/src/packet.c b/src/packet.c
index cdadefe..d957ebd 100644
--- a/src/packet.c
+++ b/src/packet.c
@@ -1586,10 +1586,14 @@ int ssh2_packet_requirev(LIBSSH2_SESSION *session,
 
         if(strchr((const char *)packet_types, ret)) {
             /* Be lazy, let packet_askv() pull it out of the brigade */
-            ret = packet_askv(session, packet_types, data, data_len,
-                              match_ofs, match_buf, match_len);
-            state->start = 0;
-            return ret;
+            if(packet_askv(session, packet_types, data, data_len,
+                           match_ofs, match_buf, match_len) == 0) {
+                state->start = 0;
+                return 0;
+            }
+            /* Waycar patch: a wanted packet type that does not match, such
+               as another channel's reply while several channels wait for
+               theirs; it stays queued for its owner. Keep reading. */
         }
     }
 
